    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract logic and real-world problem-solving—something I find both challenging and rewarding. While my parents’ education was vocational, my master’s degree required deep engagement with math concepts, which sharpened my analytical skills. Though I dislike its rigid structure, it’s an essential tool for explaining complex ideas in biology or chemistry, where precision matters.",
